{
  "scenario_name": "maian_crystal_pistol_play_smoke",
  "description": "Maian crystal pistol, first runtime proof of the custom weapon mod: one ordinary client launch builds the mod from its recipe (dev-mods/maian_crystal_pistol) through --mod-author, the same save, validate, enable and apply path the in-game creators use, then starts a solo Combat match on Felicity with the pistol in the player's hand, fires the primary three times, switches the fire mode and fires the secondary once. It proves that the recipe builds in the game, that the weapon is found, loaded and equipped with the mod's own mesh, that the first primary shot loads the crystal's own mesh, and that firing both functions neither crashes nor ends the match. It does not prove that a crystal is seen, sticks or detonates: no log line states a projectile spawn or an attach, and in the first run (2026-11-15) neither the placeholder gun nor a crystal was visible in the four screenshots. The cluster rule, the charge, per-socket launch, regrowth and ammo wait for graph support.",
